# Text Sanitizer Function

Here's a self-contained JavaScript function using the `Intl.Segmenter` API (standardized in 2024) to handle text sanitization:

```javascript
/**
 * Sanitizes input text to contain only alphabetic characters, digits, and spaces
 * @param {string} text - The input text to sanitize
 * @returns {string} - Sanitized text with only A-Z, a-z, 0-9, and spaces
 */
function sanitizeText(text) {
  // Use Intl.Segmenter to properly handle Unicode grapheme clusters
  const segmenter = new Intl.Segmenter(undefined, { granularity: 'grapheme' });

  const segments = segmenter.segment(text);
  const result = [];

  for (const { segment } of segments) {
    const charCode = segment.charCodeAt(0);

    // Keep A-Z (65-90), a-z (97-122), 0-9 (48-57), and space (32)
    if (
      (charCode >= 65 && charCode <= 90) ||   // A-Z
      (charCode >= 97 && charCode <= 122) ||  // a-z
      (charCode >= 48 && charCode <= 57) ||   // 0-9
      charCode === 32                          // space
    ) {
      result.push(segment);
    }
  }

  return result.join('');
}

